    # 'struct'". Upstream's test is `[(); size_of::<&Self>()]` / `[(); foo::<&'a ()>()]`,
    # so neither annotated half has a shape here. To make it a row: it is a LANGUAGE
    # feature request, not a defect — decide with the owner whether const-expression array
    # lengths are wanted at all before this is priced.

enum_payload_nested_pattern_absent defect 1  tests/imported/admit/nll/enum-drop-access
    # 2026-09-07 — MISSING FEATURE, blocking a re-port. `match opt { DropOption::Some(&mut ref mut r) => .. }`
    # reports "pattern DropOption::Some: nested patterns inside enum-variant payloads are not
    # yet supported; bind to a name and match in the body". The generic enum with a `Drop` impl
    # compiles on its own, so it is the nested pattern alone that has no path. The row
    # `enum-drop-access` sits in bc_admits_blocked as BUCKET-4 because upstream's whole test IS
    # the reborrow-through-the-payload `&mut ref mut r`. To make it a row: decide whether this is
    # the same missing Struct/Ref arm as soundness_queue `match_tuple_door_nested_struct_binds_nothing`
    # and `let_at_binding_tuple_sub_unsupported` (doors in SERIES on ONE reader) or a third door —
    # if one reader, these are one row, not three.

